# LRC14 fibbinary/Moser partial-cube and edge-sector scout

## Ordered edge-sector / doubled-triangular row
k  simplex_edges=C(k,2)  ordered_sectors=k(k-1)=2*T_{k-1}
 2                     1                                   2
 3                     3                                   6
 4                     6                                  12
 5                    10                                  20
 6                    15                                  30
 7                    21                                  42

sequence k=2..7: [2, 6, 12, 20, 30, 42]
origin: ordered 1-faces of the (k-1)-simplex, not a raw LRC proof.

## Fibonacci cubes Gamma_n
n  vertices=F_{n+2}  edges  layers C(n-r+1,r) over independent r-sets
 1                2      1 [1,1]
 2                3      2 [1,2]
 3                5      5 [1,3,1]
 4                8     10 [1,4,3]
 5               13     20 [1,5,6,1]
 6               21     38 [1,6,10,4]
 7               34     71 [1,7,15,10,1]
 8               55    130 [1,8,21,20,5]

## Moser-de Bruijn even-bit cubes M_m embedded in Gamma_{2m-1}
m  bit_length  vertices=2^m  cube_edges=m*2^(m-1)  layers C(m,r)
 1           1             2                      1 [1,1]
 2           3             4                      4 [1,2,1]
 3           5             8                     12 [1,3,3,1]
 4           7            16                     32 [1,4,6,4,1]
 5           9            32                     80 [1,5,10,10,5,1]
 6          11            64                    192 [1,6,15,20,15,6,1]
 7          13           128                    448 [1,7,21,35,35,21,7,1]

## Inclusion and transition guardrails
M_1 subset Gamma_1: 2/2 vertices retained
M_2 subset Gamma_3: 4/5 vertices retained
M_3 subset Gamma_5: 8/13 vertices retained
M_4 subset Gamma_7: 16/34 vertices retained
M_5 subset Gamma_9: 32/89 vertices retained
M_6 subset Gamma_11: 64/233 vertices retained

transition facts:
- fibbinary is closed under x -> 2x by appending a zero bit.
- Moser is closed under x -> 4x by appending a base-4 zero digit.
- Moser is not closed under x -> 2x unless the even/odd bit phase is retained.

